{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Besides what his hand can attain.</b> If he said 'I am a nazirite on condition that I shave upon one hundred burnt-offerings and one hundred peace-offerings,' 'according to his vow that he vows, so he shall do' — an addition to the law of his naziriteship: upon the law of the nazirite, an addition and not a subtraction. For if he said 'I am a nazirite for five naziriteships on condition that I shave upon these three animals,' I do not apply to him 'according to what he vows, so he shall do.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:46.052717938Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}